program            = 007_extension_keyword
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = GCC __extension__ suppressing pedantic rejection of statement expressions, typeof declarations and long long constants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
UB-GATE DEVIATION AND ITS REASON. Every program in area 08_gcc_extensions drops
-pedantic from the default warning gate. Reason: the constructs under test are
non-standard GCC extensions by definition, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
them; retaining it would fail every program in the area for doing exactly what it is
meant to do. This is the only area-wide deviation in the corpus. No other warning is
relaxed: -Wall, -Wextra, -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion, -Wshadow and -Werror are all
retained, and this program is clean under them at -O0, -O1 and -O2. Measured with
gcc 13.3.0.

A NOTE SPECIFIC TO THIS PROGRAM. Because __extension__ exists precisely to suppress the
pedantic diagnostics that the area-wide deviation also removes, this program was
additionally validated WITH -pedantic added, and it is clean. That is the demonstration
that the keyword genuinely suppresses. Measured control with gcc 13.3.0: the same braced
group WITHOUT __extension__, compiled with -pedantic -Werror, produces "error: ISO C
forbids braced-groups within expressions [-Werror=pedantic]". Within the suite the
observable assertion is that the wrapped constructs compile and behave correctly, which
oracle a and oracle b both verify from the printed output.

UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. There is no signed overflow: the int computations are 4+9, 13*2,
6*6+1, 4*3+1 and 13+87, all tiny, and the long long values 1234567890123 and
1000000000000+23 are far from the 64-bit limits. No shift operator is used. No pointer,
array or aggregate is used, so there is no aliasing violation and no one-past-end pointer.
Every object is initialized before it is read, including every statement-expression local.
No object is modified twice between sequence points. Every printf call receives at most one
side-effecting argument. Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the addresses of unrelated
objects.

MACRO LOCAL NAMES ARE DISJOINT AND NO MACRO IS NESTED INSIDE ITSELF. This is the hazard
that broke an earlier draft of this program: EXT_MAX(EXT_MAX(1, 7), 5) produces "error:
declaration of 'ext_max_x_' shadows a previous local [-Werror=shadow]", because the inner
expansion's locals shadow the outer's. -Wshadow is in the area gate and -Werror makes it
fatal. Two differently named macros therefore exist: EXT_MAX uses ext_max_x_ and
ext_max_y_, EXT_MIN uses ext_min_p_ and ext_min_q_, so the nesting
EXT_MAX(EXT_MIN(7, 1), 5) is safe. Every inline statement expression likewise has a
uniquely suffixed local.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed, so no target restriction is needed and all
four targets are compared.

long long is used throughout, never long, and the matching specifier is %lld, never %ld.
long long is 64-bit on all four targets, whereas long was measured as 4 bytes on i686 and
8 bytes on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64. Both printed 64-bit values, 1234567890123 and
1000000000023, exceed 32 bits, so long would overflow on i686 and manufacture a divergence
caused by the test rather than the compiler.

Plain char is never used, so the measured char-signedness difference cannot be reached:
char is signed on x86_64 and i686 but unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. No address or
pointer value is printed.

__extension__ is exercised in three distinct grammatical positions: before a statement
expression in value position, before a declaration including a __typeof__ declaration, and
before a parenthesized ordinary expression. All three are legitimate and all three are
retained deliberately.

The runtime variant is driven by volatile int and volatile long long operands so the
optimizer cannot fold the computation and must emit genuine instructions, while the folded
variant exercises the constant folder. EXT_MAX is called once without a cast on a volatile
operand and EXT_MIN once with an explicit (int) cast, so both spellings are covered; the
cast reads the volatile object once and yields a plain int, which avoids declaring a
volatile-qualified local inside the macro via __typeof__ of a volatile lvalue.

The unsigned conversion is written with an explicit (unsigned) cast so -Wconversion and
-Wsign-conversion stay quiet under -Werror; the value 13+87 is 100, comfortably in range.

__extension__ is documented as supported at docs/technical-specifications.md lines 98, 107
and 761, so this program tests documented functionality and carries NO
expected-divergence marker.

Output is identical on all four targets at all three optimization levels.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
ext_folded_stmt=13
ext_folded_ll=1234567890123
ext_folded_typeof=26
ext_folded_ull=100
ext_folded_max=9
ext_folded_min=4
ext_folded_nested=5
ext_folded_scale=13
ext_folded_arg=10
ext_runtime_stmt=37
ext_runtime_max=11
ext_runtime_min=6
ext_runtime_ll=1000000000023
ext_runtime_scale=19
END
